{% comment %}
One compliance framework as the trust center shows it.

Expects `catalog_summary`, one entry from
`controls.services.public_service.get_public_controls_list`.

Two decisions worth keeping:

**Domains, not every control.** A framework is a few hundred controls and a
visitor is asking one question: how far along is this programme. The domain
breakdown answers that in a screen; the full control list is a spreadsheet and
belongs in the app, where the people who own it work.

**No severity colours on a score.** Red means critical on every trust center,
and an amber 60% would borrow that meaning for something that is not a
vulnerability. A domain that is fully addressed gets the success tone and
everything else stays neutral, so the colour says "finished" rather than
grading someone's programme in public.
{% endcomment %}
<c-branded.surface flush>
<div class="flex [flex-wrap:wrap] items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-4 border-b border-solid border-border">
    <div class="min-w-0 flex flex-col gap-1.5">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-text my-0">{{ catalog_summary.catalog.name }}</p>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 [flex-wrap:wrap]">
            {% if catalog_summary.catalog.version %}
                <c-branded.badge>{{ catalog_summary.catalog.version }}</c-branded.badge>
            {% endif %}
            {% if catalog_summary.catalog.is_synced %}
                {% comment %}
                Where the numbers come from. A visitor treats "kept current by
                the tool that runs this programme" differently from a figure
                somebody typed, so the page says which it is looking at.
                {% endcomment %}
                <c-branded.badge title="Kept up to date automatically">
                <i class="fas fa-arrows-rotate" aria-hidden="true"></i>Synced from {{ catalog_summary.catalog.source_label }}
                </c-branded.badge>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    </div>
    <c-branded.stats>
    <c-branded.stat label="Addressed">{{ catalog_summary.percentage|floatformat:0 }}%</c-branded.stat>
    <c-branded.stat label="of {{ catalog_summary.total }} control{{ catalog_summary.total|pluralize }}">{{ catalog_summary.addressed|floatformat:"-1" }}</c-branded.stat>
    </c-branded.stats>
</div>
{% for category in catalog_summary.categories %}
    <c-branded.list-row>
    <c-slot name="heading">{{ category.name }}</c-slot>
    <c-slot name="side">
    {% if category.total and category.addressed >= category.total %}
        <c-branded.badge tone="success">Fully addressed</c-branded.badge>
    {% else %}
        <c-branded.badge>{{ category.percentage|floatformat:0 }}%</c-branded.badge>
    {% endif %}
    <span>{{ category.addressed|floatformat:"-1" }} of {{ category.total }}</span>
    </c-slot>
    </c-branded.list-row>
{% endfor %}
</c-branded.surface>
